# The other examples rely on the repository's root .gitignore. This one needs a
# file of its own because running it leaves two artifacts the root file does not
# mention — `.ruff_cache/` from `horus lint`/`horus fmt`, and the `horus.lock`
# that `horus run` resolves — so running the example would otherwise dirty the
# working tree.
#
# The rest matches what `horus new --python` generates, so `horus new my_robot
# --from sensor_navigation_py` hands you the same .gitignore the blank Python
# template would have.

# HORUS environment (auto-managed by `horus run`)
.horus/packages/
.horus/bin/
.horus/lib/
.horus/include/
.horus/cache/
.horus/target/
.horus/Cargo.toml
.horus/Cargo.lock
*.log
horus.lock

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
